          %h3#GelfandDuality Gelfand duality
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            between (nonunital) commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C*-algebras
            and (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"}> locally
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
          %h3#serreswan_theorem Serre-Swan theorem
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre-Swan+theorem"} Serre-Swan theorem
            says that suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over an commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C*-algebra
            are equivalently modules of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            over the
            %a{:href => "#GelfandDuality"} Gelfand-dual
            topological space.
